Z||000003||Songman||04-24-2001||08:39 PM||||Of course they will... as long as special interest groups keep running our government. So many groups get together and decide that the whole country should do things their way or they are wrong. And if they can get loud enough and get enough money behind them, then it becomes the 'politically correct' thing to do, if not the law!<P>Seems to me that the same sorta thing was happening in the past which lead to the formation of a new 'free' country. <P>Isn't it sad when the lessons of the past are forgotten and have to be learned again? Makes me wonder how many people these days thing the Holocaust and Viet Nam couldn't happen again.. or how many young ones even know what they were...<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/songman_1.gif"> <BR><A HREF="http://members.home.com/tnfieros" TARGET=_blank>Tennessee Fiero Owners</A>||||reg||1
